  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each statement.\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(-\\infty ,-2].$ Although the function is continuous on $(-\\infty ,-2),$ it is not left-continuous at $x=-2.$\n\n- The function is continuous on $[-2,4].$ It is continuous on $(-2,4),$ and also right-continuous at $x=-2$ and left-continuous at $x=4.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $[4,\\infty ).$ Although the function is continuous on $(4,\\infty ),$ it is not right-continuous at $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
